{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 12, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "Arthur awoke to the smell of pine needles and damp earth. Sunlight dappled through the leaves of towering trees, painting shifting patterns on the forest floor. He stretched, a familiar ache in his back, and reached for his glasses on the bedside table. Except, the bedside table wasn't there. Instead, he was surrounded by a vibrant, impossibly green forest, the air thick with the sound of birdsong he'd never heard before. He glanced down at his hands – calloused and strong, but strangely… pixelated? A flicker of confusion morphed into a chilling realization. The trees weren't just trees; they were rendered with painstaking detail, the leaves shimmering with an unnatural glow. A small, wooden signpost stood nearby, displaying a crudely drawn map and the words \"Whispering Woods - Level 1.\" Arthur stared, his mind reeling. This wasn't his bedroom. This wasn't reality. He was inside a video game.\n\n***\n\nPanic clawed at his throat. He tried to speak, but only a raspy whisper escaped. He ran a hand through his hair, feeling the coarse texture of what felt like… cloth? His clothes weren't his usual worn jeans and t-shirt. He was wearing a simple tunic and leather boots. The vibrant colors, the flawless graphics, the utterly artificial nature of everything screamed \"simulation.\"  He noticed a small, ornate sword lying half-hidden beneath a cluster of ferns.  A quest? A tutorial?  The possibilities, terrifying and exhilarating in equal measure, flooded his consciousness.  He took a shaky breath, a newfound determination hardening his gaze.  He had to figure out how to get out, how to break free from this digital prison, but first, he had a feeling he needed to level up.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.7662928104400635}, {"token": "▁awoke", "logprob": -0.4878727197647095}, {"token": "▁to", "logprob": -0.0028092702850699425}, {"token"